WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.675
Twin screws change everything, and once you learn them, you’ll never want one engine again.

2
00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:12.075
Most twin-screw boats have counter-rotating propellers, so each one cancels the other’s walk.

3
00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:17.000
Put one engine ahead and the other astern, and the boat spins in place.

4
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.775
Which way?

5
00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:20.675
Think of a tank.

6
00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:25.825
Starboard engine ahead, port engine astern, and the bow swings to port.

7
00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:28.900
Swap them, and it swings to starboard.

8
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:33.150
Around the docks, center the rudders and leave the wheel alone.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.275
Steer with the engines.

10
00:00:35.525 --> 00:00:39.325
And use small bursts, with plenty of neutral in between.

11
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:42.250
What’s the commonest mistake with twins?

12
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.125
Leaving them in gear.

13
00:00:45.375 --> 00:00:52.350
A boat keeps moving long after you take her out of gear, so click in, click out, and wait to see what she does.
